<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21165] lctl del_ost always prints usage on aarch64</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21165</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;jt_del_ost() stores the getopt_long() return value in a "char c". On architectures where plain char is unsigned (aarch64, ppc64le) c never equals -1, so the option loop runs past the last option into "default: return CMD_HELP", and "lctl del_ost -n -t FSNAME-OST0000" always prints the usage message.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;conf-sanity test_123ah fails on aarch64 servers with:&lt;br/&gt;
  del_ost --dryrun failed with 4&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;x86_64 is not affected because char is signed there. The variable should be an int.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Introduced by commit 1121816c4a4e ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-7668" title="permanently remove deactivated OSTs from configuration log" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-7668"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-7668&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; utils: add lctl del_ost").&lt;/p&gt;</description>
